            <ArticleTitle>Recanalization of iatrogenic dissection of the superior mesenteric artery: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>314-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/1538574413485647</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of acute abdominal pain due to a long-segment iatrogenic superior mesenteric artery dissection, which was immediately treated successfully with balloon fenestration of the intimal flap, resulting in complete resolution of the symptoms without recurrence during the 2-year follow-up period.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
